  "result": "Perfect! VAT report is complete. All 266 tests pass.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **vatSummary(invoices)** function in src/reports.js that:\n   - Filters invoices for status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' (excludes draft)\n   - Processes all line items across included invoices\n   - For each line, calculates:\n     - `base` = line total minus line discount (the taxable amount)\n     - `vat` = the VAT already calculated per-line (and rounded)\n   - Groups and accumulates by VAT rate\n   - Returns array of `{ rate, base, vat }` objects\n   - Sorted by rate descending (high to low)\n\n2. **14 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - Empty invoice lists\n   - Draft invoice exclusion (included status: issued, partially_paid, paid)\n   - Single and multiple VAT rates\n   - Rate sorting (21%, 0%, etc. high to low)\n   - Line discounts reducing the base but not affecting VAT rate\n   - VAT-exempt products (0% rate with 0 VAT)\n   - Accumulation across multiple invoices\n   - Multiple VAT rates in a single invoice\n   - Complex invoices with mixed rates and discounts\n   - Edge cases (one rate only, multiple discounted lines)\n\nThe VAT report provides a breakdown of taxable bases and VAT amounts by rate, useful for VAT reporting and reconciliation.",
